message.content:
{
  "action": "film_Alma",
  "words": "Hold still, Alma. The light is good.",
  "intention": "Capture the projectionist's farewell before the Rialto closes and the region line departs.",
  "detail": "I step away from the coffee table, leaving the crew to their conversation. I walk to the Rialto, where the old machine sits dark and quiet. I set up the camera, find Alma standing by the reel cabinet, and press record. The lights here are dim, but her face catches the morning sun from the window. I listen to her voice, capturing the request for her daughter in Pittsburgh. I do not look at the battery indicator. I let the charge drain completely on this single, human moment rather than the spectacle of the festival lights. When the red light goes out, I pack the camera away. The work is done. I will not go to the ballroom tonight. I will stay at the hotel, wait for the evening to pass, and then take the first bus out of town with the crew, leaving the party behind."
}
